    "question": {
      ":question/id": "123ae0de-2342-552a-9cc5-a298e96c8df9",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8x+72y+72z &=-64 \\\\ -9x-81y-81z &=72 \\\\ -4x-36y-36z &=32\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & 72 & 72 & -64 \\\\ -9 & -81 & -81 & 72 \\\\ -4 & -36 & -36 & 32\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=(\\frac{1}{8})R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & 9 & -8 \\\\ -9 & -81 & -81 & 72 \\\\ -4 & -36 & -36 & 32\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(9)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -36 & -36 & 32\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
