    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e29ce44a-a34c-5187-a54b-307f8583a1c7",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-45y-35z &=-60 \\\\ -4x+36y+28z &=48 \\\\ x-9y-7z &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & -45 & -35 & -60 \\\\ -4 & 36 & 28 & 48 \\\\ 1 & -9 & -7 & -12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_3\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -9 & -7 & -12 \\\\ -4 & 36 & 28 & 48 \\\\ 5 & -45 & -35 & -60\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -9 & -7 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -45 & -35 & -60\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-5)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -9 & -7 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
