    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9eaf3c32-a35c-59d3-919f-cafb73ae50bc",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+54y+24z &=-72 \\\\ -8x-72y-32z &=96 \\\\ x+9y+4z &=-12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & 54 & 24 & -72 \\\\ -8 & -72 & -32 & 96 \\\\ 1 & 9 & 4 & -12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_3\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & 4 & -12 \\\\ -8 & -72 & -32 & 96 \\\\ 6 & 54 & 24 & -72\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(8)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 54 & 24 & -72\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-6)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 9 & 4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
