    "question": {
      ":question/id": "68c19d9d-6527-5106-9f11-42a18b1950dc",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+7y-56z &=-35 \\\\ x+y-8z &=-5 \\\\ 10x+10y-80z &=-50\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}7 & 7 & -56 & -35 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -8 & -5 \\\\ 10 & 10 & -80 & -50\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_2\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -8 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 7 & -56 & -35 \\\\ 10 & 10 & -80 & -50\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-7)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 10 & 10 & -80 & -50\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-10)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & -8 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
